5. CODEPILOT BRANDING
============================================================

CodePilot Branding is expressly excluded from the general permissions
granted under this license, except for the limited permissions expressly
stated in this section.

The complete CodePilot Software package may contain official branding.
The original branding may remain intact when a user retains, uses, modifies,
backs up, or privately shares a permitted copy of the complete package.

However, this license does NOT grant permission to independently extract,
publish, redistribute, sell, or reuse CodePilot logos and branding images.

Unless separately authorized by the Rights Holder or otherwise permitted
by applicable law, you may NOT:

a. Distribute CodePilot logos or branding images as standalone assets.

b. Use CodePilot Branding as the official identity of another product,
project, organization, or service.

c. Claim CodePilot Branding as your own.

d. Falsely imply that a product or project is officially affiliated with,
sponsored by, approved by, or endorsed by CodePilot.

e. Remove or alter applicable ownership notices for the purpose of
misrepresenting the origin of the Branding.

f. Sell or independently redistribute official CodePilot Branding.

Separate permission is required for uses of excluded Branding that are
not otherwise permitted by applicable law.

Third-party branding and assets remain subject to their respective owners'
rights and licensing terms.

