7. ENFORCEMENT AND RIGHTS PROTECTION
============================================================

Where legally justified, the Rights Holder reserves the right to choose
appropriate actions in response to unauthorized publication, public
redistribution, sale, or misuse of protected CodePilot Branding.

Depending on the circumstances and applicable law, possible actions include:

a. RTBF (Right to Be Forgotten) requests where applicable to personal
information and supported by the relevant legal grounds.

b. Cease-and-desist (C/D) notices.

c. Copyright or trademark complaints and takedown requests where legally
justified.

d. Requests to correct or remove material that unlawfully misuses protected
Branding or misrepresents an official affiliation.

e. Other legal or administrative remedies available under applicable law.

The Rights Holder may select one or more available actions depending on
the circumstances. No action is guaranteed to succeed, and all actions
remain subject to applicable law and the facts of the situation.

Nothing in this license creates a legal right to submit a request that
would otherwise be unavailable under applicable law.

An RTBF request is intended for applicable personal-information and privacy
situations. It is not, by itself, a general mechanism for removing software
copies or enforcing branding restrictions.

Nothing in this section authorizes harassment, false claims, unlawful
retaliation, or misuse of reporting procedures.

